> However, any advice about what wish would make me most able to handle
> the dragons et al?

That's usually some item granting reflection, but you've already got the
SDSM. What you need now is probably either a much better AC or some fast
offensive weapon (no, I won't advise Dragonbane, even in this case). If
you didn't have reflection yet, I'd say try Sokoban first, but that
won't be necessary now.

> I'm kind of thinking to sacrifice until I get
> magicbane and then wish for speed boots...but maybe a spellbook of
> magic missile would be better?  I do have a magic marker so I could
> write the spell book but I have no luckstone so the chances that it
> would work are bad (particularly since the moon is new.)  I'd rather
> not use the wish, with that in mind, advice?

Magicbane should come fast, it's a guaranteed first gift. Speed boots
are always a good choice: theyt'll not only help against those dragons,
but they'll last throughout the entire game, if you survive the dragons.

Talking about patience, you can always start up another game and return
to your wizard when the moon has come to her senses again.

Lastly, since you have reflection, you might want to try to get the
critters to approach you in a long, straight corridor, the vampire in
front if possible, and let them breathe at you, destroying the other
critters in front of you while they do so.

Meanwhile, you can cast spells at them, and retreat to the stairs when
you're running out of mana.

